  "adaptive_lift_a4b3": "Project onto three singleton targets and three pair targets. The independently replayed old a3b3 strategy identifies this projection in four queries. Complement any query with more than five selected candidates, pad its k<=5 selected candidates with M-k known nonmembers, and restore h to n-h for complemented targets before traversing the old tree. The a4b3 encoder has M in 5..8, so 0..8 known-negative padding rows suffice. In parallel, query the fourth singleton with the balanced four-bit unique candidate code. Decode all seven counts using the audited a4b3 exact mean alphabet. This covers every legal a4b3 assignment; no adaptive search is run for fixed-SAT types.",
